## 🧠 The Secret to Becoming a Great Bug Bounty Hunter
Bad hackers try to memorize random exploit payloads they copy off the internet. Great bug bounty hunters master the underlying architectural rules.
When you understand the exact laws of how a Linux terminal handles a newline character (\n), or how a database columns layout must match during a UNION statement, you don't need a cheat sheet. You can look at a target web application, figure out how the developer structured their backend code rules, and craft a completely unique payload to break it.
